IsdaYou — Build Checklist (Manuscript-Aligned)
This replaces the previous checklist. Every step below is cross-referenced to the
manuscript requirement it implements, so if a requirement changes later, you know
exactly which build step to revisit.

What changed from the last version, and why:
The pipeline is now single-stage, not two-stage — matching Section 9.3, Section 3.2
(Out of Scope: "Multiple Fish Detection and Counting"), Section 3.4, and MLR-001
through MLR-016. There is no YOLO detection/cropping stage. The manuscript states
the team deliberately chose CNN-only single-label classification over a
detection-based pipeline, because the app's use case assumes one user-framed fish
per photo — adding detection was judged unnecessary overhead for the target
hardware and offline constraints. This is a correction, not a simplification: the
previous "two-model" version contradicted the manuscript outright.

Geofencing still runs offline, against locally cached boundary data — matching
Section 5.3. Only refreshing that data (via the BFAR scraper) needs internet;
checking a user's location against it does not. This part was already correct and
is unchanged.

Android's dedicated Geofencing API is still required for FR-016's background
detection — Fused Location Provider alone can't do this. Also unchanged.

Terminology matches the manuscript: "restricted area" (the general term used
throughout Section 3.1, covering MPAs and other regulated zones) and "closed
season," not "breeding alerts" / "breeding zone."

Python pinned to a safer version range for the ML tooling — now justified by
TensorFlow/Keras and TFLite export tooling compatibility, not Ultralytics (which
is no longer part of the stack, since there's no YOLO model to train).
=======================================================================================================================================================
Hybrid Offline/Online Mode — the source of truth for every step below
Offline (no internet) — matches Section 5.3, "Offline Continuity with Periodic Synchronization":
- Fish identification: single CNN classifies the full submitted image on-device via TFLite (no detection/crop stage)
- Species library lookup: cached `FishSpecies` data in Room/SQLite
- Restricted-area / closed-season checks: `RestrictedArea.containsLocation()` evaluated against locally cached boundary and date-range data in Room
- Catch and identification logging: saved locally in Room, queued for sync

Online (internet available) — matches Section 5.3's sync clause, BR10, and FR-024:
- `GovernmentDataSource` scraper refreshes `RestrictedArea` boundaries, closed-season date ranges, and species data from BFAR sources (web scraping where no formal API exists)
- `WorkManager` uploads queued `FishImage` / `FishIdentification` logs, subject to user consent (MLR-016)
- Notifications about newly changed rules can push once refreshed data lands, but the check itself never depends on connectivity

Keep this distinction in mind through every step — it's the one design point most likely to quietly drift if a step gets written without checking it.
