## 6. Build the backend and the government data scraper

6.1. In `backend/`: `python -m venv venv`
6.2. `pip install fastapi uvicorn sqlalchemy psycopg2-binary beautifulsoup4 requests celery`
6.3. Build the scraper (`GovernmentDataSource`) targeting BFAR/DA advisory pages to pull closed-season date ranges (`startDate`, `endDate`) and 
     restricted-area updates — matches FR-024's "automated data ingestion pipeline, including web scraping where no formal data feed is available"
6.4. Schedule it with APScheduler or Celery, running `GovernmentDataSource.getUpdates()` to refresh `RestrictedArea` records in PostGIS — this is the online-only half of the system; 
     nothing about running the check itself should live here
6.5. Expose sync endpoints: `/api/v1/sync/species`, `/api/v1/sync/geofences`, `/api/v1/notifications`

