## 7. Build the mobile app (Android — Kotlin)

7.1. In Android Studio: new project in `mobile-app/`, Kotlin, minimum SDK API 28
7.2. Add dependencies in `build.gradle`:
     - CameraX — capturing/selecting a `FishImage`
     - TensorFlow Lite Android — runs `species_classifier.tflite`
     - Room — offline cache for `FishSpecies`, `FishIdentification`, `RestrictedArea` boundaries and closed-season dates, and queued logs
     - Retrofit + OkHttp — sync calls to the backend when online
     - Play Services Location (Fused Location Provider) — current device coordinates
     - Play Services Geofencing API (`GeofencingClient`) — location alone only tells you where you are; 
       the Geofencing API is what lets the OS notify your app when a boundary is entered or approached, including while the app isn't in the foreground, which is what FR-016 actually requires
     - WorkManager — background sync when connectivity returns
     - Jetpack Compose — UI
7.3. Place `species_classifier.tflite` and `labels.txt` in `app/src/main/assets/`
7.4. Build CameraX capture/gallery-select flow
7.5. Implement the full local pipeline, matching MLR-001 through MLR-016:
      Capture or select image (MLR-001)
      → Validate resolution/format, reject invalid input (MLR-002)
      → Preprocess: resize to CNN input dimensions, normalize pixel values (MLR-003)
      → CNN classifies the full image directly — no crop step (MLR-004)
      → Return species class + confidence score (MLR-005)
      → Threshold filter: only show results meeting the primary confidence threshold (MLR-006)
      → Below threshold: "no confident identification" (MLR-008), not a species name
      → Show up to 3 ranked alternative candidates above the secondary threshold (MLR-007)
      → Display result with an "assistive, not certified taxonomic determination" advisory (MLR-009)
      → Display the submitted image next to the result so the user can visually confirm it (MLR-010)
      → Let the user reject the result and manually pick the correct species from the library (MLR-011)
      → Log timestamp, predicted class, confidence, and any user correction (MLR-012)
      → Link the confirmed identification to its species profile — protection status shown regardless of location — and to any applicable zone/season advisory (MLR-013)
      → Record the active model's version identifier with the prediction (MLR-014)
7.6. Implement `RestrictedArea.containsLocation()` to run locally, against Room's cached boundary and closed-season data, using coordinates from 
     the Fused Location Provider and boundary entry/exit events from the Geofencing API — this must work with the phone in airplane mode
7.7. Design the model layer so `species_classifier.tflite` can be swapped for a retrained version without touching other modules (MLR-015) 
     — keep the TFLite file, `labels.txt`, and the code that loads them decoupled from the rest of the app
