## 11. Testing and validation

11.1. AI accuracy — test with unseen fish photos; check overall accuracy, precision, recall, F1, and Top-3 accuracy per Section 10.1.1, 
      plus the per-species recall floor for closed-season/protected species (Section 5.2). Also check whether higher-confidence predictions are actually more often correct (Section 10.1.2) — 
      - a confidence score that doesn't track real reliability is a UX problem, not just a metrics one
11.2. Offline integrity — airplane mode: confirm camera capture, classification, species library, and restricted-area/closed-season checks all still work with zero connectivity
11.3. Geofencing correctness — with cached boundary data already on the device, simulate coordinates inside a restricted area, in airplane mode, and confirm the alert still fires
11.4. Scraper test — trigger `GovernmentDataSource.getUpdates()` manually, confirm BFAR data populates `RestrictedArea` correctly
11.5. Sync queue — scan offline, reconnect, confirm `WorkManager` uploads without duplicating records, and only after consent is given
11.6. Framing sensitivity — since there's no detection/cropping stage, deliberately test off-center, partially obstructed, and cluttered-background 
      photos to see how much accuracy degrades (Section 3.4 flags this as an expected limitation, not a bug)
11.7. Track every bug in GitHub Issues

